{"_id":"6a2fefe82204ffbc59e5a3ac","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"-RepeaHp66GGuM66k9JHd","description":"# sqlite3\n\n`sqlite3` is Python's built-in library for working with SQLite databases. SQLite is a lightweight, file-based relational database that requires no server setup. It is commonly used for local data storage, prototyping, and working with small to medium datasets entirely within Python.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"sqlite3","url":"https://docs.python.org/3/library/sqlite3.html#sqlite3-tutorial","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb80"},{"type":"video","title":"Sqlite 3 Python Tutorial in 5 minutes","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=girsuXz0yA8","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb81"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:28:24.170Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/-RepeaHp66GGuM66k9JHd.md"}